# How to cite ARPES viewer: read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by
# Zenodo when it archives a release. The DOI is Zenodo's concept DOI: it
# stands for all versions and resolves to the latest. The licence is the
# SPDX id Zenodo maps to its own entry, so each archived release carries it
# rather than Zenodo's default (CC BY 4.0, which would allow commercial use).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ARPES viewer for a paper, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ARPES viewer"
abstract: >-
  A Python/PyQt5 program for angle-resolved photoemission (ARPES) data:
  browse the measurements of a beamtime, convert to momentum, cut, fit,
  process, compare with band-structure calculations, and lay the results
  out as publication figures.
authors:
  - family-names: Pei
    given-names: Ding
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3995-0690"
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
version: 1.2.2
date-released: 2026-10-29
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23771647
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23771647
    description: "Concept DOI: all versions, resolving to the latest"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DingPei1995/ARPES-data-browser"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/arpes-viewer/"
keywords:
  - ARPES
  - photoemission
  - synchrotron
  - band structure
  - Fermi surface
